\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Effect of each action on traffic flow. Each panel is one junction seen top-down, the arterial running left to right with the cross street joining from above. In every panel the left of the stop line is the state at the decision instant (\textit  {now}: hollow glyphs) and the right is the same stream after the action (\textit  {after}: filled glyphs); the light pair at the top right is the \textit  {current aspect}, main then cross, so the reader can see the light the action is taken on together with the flow it changes. (a) With no intervention the bus waits out the red and the queue behind it grows. (b) \texttt  {GE} widens the arterial's green window by $\delta $, so the bus clears without stopping. (c) \texttt  {GR} truncates the cross-street green by $\delta $, bringing the bus green forward. (d) \texttt  {INS} adds a bus phase to the ring, so the bus is served this cycle instead of the next. (e) \texttt  {ER} ends the bus phase once the bus has cleared, handing green to the cross street early. (f) \texttt  {VP} drops an empty phase from the ring, removing two lost reds per cycle. (g) \texttt  {PT} re-sequences the ring so the bus phase is served first. (h) Offset correction shifts the upstream green band by $\Delta $ so the bus arrives on green. Panels are schematic and carry no measured values. Panel (b) is enlarged in \cref  {fig:ge_wave}.}}{7}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:action_mech}{{1}{7}{Effect of each action on traffic flow. Each panel is one junction seen top-down, the arterial running left to right with the cross street joining from above. In every panel the left of the stop line is the state at the decision instant (\textit {now}: hollow glyphs) and the right is the same stream after the action (\textit {after}: filled glyphs); the light pair at the top right is the \textit {current aspect}, main then cross, so the reader can see the light the action is taken on together with the flow it changes. (a) With no intervention the bus waits out the red and the queue behind it grows. (b) \texttt {GE} widens the arterial's green window by $\delta $, so the bus clears without stopping. (c) \texttt {GR} truncates the cross-street green by $\delta $, bringing the bus green forward. (d) \texttt {INS} adds a bus phase to the ring, so the bus is served this cycle instead of the next. (e) \texttt {ER} ends the bus phase once the bus has cleared, handing green to the cross street early. (f) \texttt {VP} drops an empty phase from the ring, removing two lost reds per cycle. (g) \texttt {PT} re-sequences the ring so the bus phase is served first. (h) Offset correction shifts the upstream green band by $\Delta $ so the bus arrives on green. Panels are schematic and carry no measured values. Panel (b) is enlarged in \cref {fig:ge_wave}}{figure.caption.3}{}}
\newlabel{fig:action_mech@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][6][]7}}
\citation{Long2022PhaseSkipping}
\citation{Long2022PhaseSkipping}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces What the green extension does to the coordinated band (schematic, one cycle repeated). Green bars are the coordinated main-street green at three junctions in route order; red is the rest of the cycle. Dots mark the bus at each junction, coloured by the aspect it meets. (a) Without action the bus arrives at J1 after its green, is held for the red, and then meets the next band at each downstream junction, losing time at every stop. (b) With the extension the bus passes J1 inside the current band and crosses J2 and J3 without stopping. The downstream bands are unchanged: the extension removes the stop and keeps the bus in the wave, which is the time it saves.}}{8}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ge_wave}{{2}{8}{What the green extension does to the coordinated band (schematic, one cycle repeated). Green bars are the coordinated main-street green at three junctions in route order; red is the rest of the cycle. Dots mark the bus at each junction, coloured by the aspect it meets. (a) Without action the bus arrives at J1 after its green, is held for the red, and then meets the next band at each downstream junction, losing time at every stop. (b) With the extension the bus passes J1 inside the current band and crosses J2 and J3 without stopping. The downstream bands are unchanged: the extension removes the stop and keeps the bus in the wave, which is the time it saves}{figure.caption.4}{}}
\newlabel{fig:ge_wave@cref}{{[figure][2][]2}{[1][6][]8}}
