\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Kelvin Grove measured queues through the run (five-seed mean, 3-min moving average). Top: absolute total queue at fixed-time and under the bus-first game. Bottom: change against fixed-time at the same junction and time; blue is a shorter queue than fixed-time, red a longer one. J5 is the persistent bottleneck in every arm; M5 shortens it in mid-run, while M4 shifts queue to J2--J3 from about 25\,min. The dark block at J12 in the final 15\,min appears in all arms, including fixed-time, and is an end-of-window boundary effect rather than a treatment effect.}}{33}{figure.caption.85}\protected@file@percent }
